-- title:
--   Proposition 4.8 — successive shrinking: with probability $\ge1-mLe^{-\gamma}$, residuals $\le\eta$ force $\|g_i\|\le\eta(1+\beta Q_L)^L$
-- statement:
--   Fix a candidate space $G_0\subseteq W=\bigoplus_{i=1}^mW_i$ of dimension at most $N_G$. For each block $\ell\in[L]$, conditioned on the earlier blocks, the $\zeta^{(\ell)}_i\in U^{(\ell)}_i$ ($i\in[m]$) are independent, each with a $(1/4,\eta_0,\gamma)$-subspace anticoncentrated law; the random linear maps $C^{(\ell)}_i:G_0\to U^{(\ell)}_i\otimes W_i$ depend only on $\{\zeta^{(\ell')}_j:\ell'<\ell\ \text{or}\ (\ell'=\ell,\ j\ne i)\}$. Let $n_{\ell i}=\dim U^{(\ell)}_i\ge4$, and suppose
--   $$Q_L=\max_{\ell\in[L]}\frac{\sqrt{\sum_in_{\ell i}^2}}{\eta_0},\qquad N_G\prod_{\ell=1}^L\Big(2\sum_{i=1}^m\frac1{n_{\ell i}}\Big)<1,\qquad\|\zeta^{(\ell)}_i\|+\|C^{(\ell)}_i\|\le\beta\ \ (\forall\ell,i),$$
--   with $\beta\ge1$. Then with probability at least $1-mL\,e^{-\gamma}$, simultaneously for every $g\in G_0$ (and every tolerance $\eta\ge0$):
--   $$\forall\ell\le L\ \forall i:\ \|\zeta^{(\ell)}_i\otimes g_i+C^{(\ell)}_i(g)\|\le\eta\ \Longrightarrow\ \forall i:\ \|g_i\|\le\eta\,(1+\beta Q_L)^L.$$
--   Applied with $\zeta^{(\ell)}_i=(v^{(\ell)}_i)^{D_i}$ and the maps of Lemma 4.4, it bounds $\|g\|$ by $\|f\|$ in the proof of Theorem 4.1.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: Euclidean spaces $U$, $W$ and the tensor product $U\otimes W$ → $\mathbb R^{\iota}$, $\mathbb R^{\kappa}$ for finite index types and $\mathbb R^{\iota\times\kappa}$ with $(u\otimes w)_{(a,b)}=u_aw_b$ (`tens`); reason: every finite-dimensional real inner product space is isometric to some $\mathbb R^{\iota}$, and $\mathbb R^{\iota\times\kappa}$ with the Frobenius norm is the Hilbert tensor product
--   - encoding: "conditioned on the earlier blocks, for each $i$, $\zeta^{(\ell)}_i$ is drawn independently from a $(1/4,\eta_0,\gamma)$-subspace anticoncentrated distribution" → for $P$-almost every value $x$ of the earlier blocks, the regular conditional distribution `condDistrib` of the block $\zeta^{(\ell)}$ given them is a product $\bigotimes_i\nu_i$ of subspace anticoncentrated probability measures; reason: the regular conditional law is the meaning of "conditioned on"; independence within the block is the product form
--   - encoding: "$C^{(\ell)}_i$ depends only on $\{\zeta^{(\ell')}_j:\ell'<\ell\vee(\ell'=\ell\wedge j\ne i)\}$" → every evaluation $\omega\mapsto C^{(\ell)}_i(\omega)g$ is measurable for the σ-algebra generated by those variables; reason: a measurable function of those variables
--   - reading: condition (20), $\|\zeta^{(\ell)}_i\|+\|C^{(\ell)}_i\|\le\beta$, for random quantities → almost surely, for all $\ell,i$; reason: the more general of the two readings (surely / almost surely); p. 33 allows the bound to fail on a small event
--   - reading: "an operator norm bound $\beta\ge1$" (sentence introducing the proposition, p. 33) → hypothesis $1\le\beta$; reason: standing assumption stated with the proposition
--   - reading: $\eta$ (free in (21)) → inside the event, for every $\eta\ge0$; reason: p. 40: "The successful event in Proposition 4.8 is uniform in the residual tolerance $\eta$"
--   - encoding: $Q_L=\max_{\ell\in[L]}(\cdots)$ → `⨆ ℓ : Fin L`, which is $0$ when $L=0$; reason: the maximum of finitely many reals
--   - encoding: "with probability at least $1-mL\exp(-\gamma)$" → the (outer) measure of the failure event is at most $mLe^{-\gamma}$; reason: the event need not be measurable
-- source:
--   Bhaskara, Guo, Sinha, Srinivas, Vijayaraghavan, Approximate Syzygies of Smoothed Polynomials and Applications, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 9c17d04e…), p. 33, Proposition 4.8

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ApproxSyzygies_Smoothed_Anticoncentration

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace ApproxSyzygies.Smoothed

/-- Proposition 4.8 (p. 33): successive shrinking. Blocks `ℓ ∈ [L]`, generators `i ∈ [m]`,
`U_i^{(ℓ)} = ℝ^{ι_{ℓ i}}` of dimension `n_{ℓ i} ≥ 4`, `W = ⨁_i W_i` with `W_i = ℝ^{κ_i}`, a
candidate space `G₀ ⊆ W` of dimension at most `N_G`. Conditionally on the earlier blocks
`(ζ^{(ℓ')})_{ℓ' < ℓ}`, the block `ζ^{(ℓ)} = (ζ_i^{(ℓ)})_i` has independent coordinates, each with a
`(1/4, η₀, γ)`-subspace anticoncentrated law (a version of the regular conditional distribution
is such a product, for almost every value of the earlier blocks). Each random linear map
`C_i^{(ℓ)} : G₀ → U_i^{(ℓ)} ⊗ W_i` is a measurable function of
`{ζ_j^{(ℓ')} : ℓ' < ℓ ∨ (ℓ' = ℓ ∧ j ≠ i)}`. With `Q_L = max_ℓ √(∑_i n_{ℓ i}²)/η₀`,
`N_G ∏_ℓ (2 ∑_i 1/n_{ℓ i}) < 1`, `β ≥ 1` and `‖ζ_i^{(ℓ)}‖ + ‖C_i^{(ℓ)}‖ ≤ β` almost surely:
outside an event of probability at most `m L e^{−γ}`, for every `η ≥ 0` and every `g ∈ G₀`,
residuals `‖ζ_i^{(ℓ)} ⊗ g_i + C_i^{(ℓ)}(g)‖ ≤ η` for all `ℓ, i` imply
`‖g_i‖ ≤ η (1 + β Q_L)^L` for all `i`. -/
theorem proposition_4_8 {m L : ℕ} {ι : Fin L → Fin m → Type} [∀ ℓ i, Fintype (ι ℓ i)]
    {κ : Fin m → Type} [∀ i, Fintype (κ i)]
    (G₀ : Submodule ℝ (PiLp 2 fun i => EuclideanSpace ℝ (κ i))) (NG : ℕ)
    (hG : Module.finrank ℝ G₀ ≤ NG) (η₀ γ β : ℝ)
    {Ω : Type} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure P]
    (ζ : ∀ ℓ i, Ω → EuclideanSpace ℝ (ι ℓ i)) (hζ : ∀ ℓ i, Measurable (ζ ℓ i))
    (hcond : ∀ ℓ : Fin L,
      ∀ᵐ x ∂(P.map fun ω (ℓ' : {ℓ' : Fin L // ℓ' < ℓ}) (i : Fin m) => ζ ℓ' i ω),
        ∃ ν : ∀ i, ProbabilityMeasure (EuclideanSpace ℝ (ι ℓ i)),
          (∀ i, SubspaceAnticonc (1 / 4) η₀ γ (ν i : Measure (EuclideanSpace ℝ (ι ℓ i)))) ∧
          condDistrib (fun ω (i : Fin m) => ζ ℓ i ω)
              (fun ω (ℓ' : {ℓ' : Fin L // ℓ' < ℓ}) (i : Fin m) => ζ ℓ' i ω) P x =
            Measure.pi fun i => (ν i : Measure (EuclideanSpace ℝ (ι ℓ i))))
    (hdim : ∀ ℓ i, 4 ≤ Fintype.card (ι ℓ i))
    (C : ∀ ℓ i, Ω → (G₀ →L[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (ι ℓ i × κ i)))
    (hCmeas : ∀ ℓ i (g : G₀),
      Measurable[MeasurableSpace.comap
          (fun ω => ((fun (ℓ' : {ℓ' : Fin L // ℓ' < ℓ}) (j : Fin m) => ζ ℓ' j ω),
            (fun j : {j : Fin m // j ≠ i} => ζ ℓ j ω))) inferInstance]
        fun ω => C ℓ i ω g)
    (hprod : (NG : ℝ) * ∏ ℓ, (2 * ∑ i, (1 : ℝ) / (Fintype.card (ι ℓ i) : ℝ)) < 1)
    (hβ1 : 1 ≤ β)
    (hβ : ∀ᵐ ω ∂P, ∀ ℓ i, ‖ζ ℓ i ω‖ + ‖C ℓ i ω‖ ≤ β) :
    P {ω | ¬ ∀ (η : ℝ), 0 ≤ η → ∀ g : G₀,
          (∀ ℓ i, ‖tens (ζ ℓ i ω) ((g : PiLp 2 fun i => EuclideanSpace ℝ (κ i)) i) +
              C ℓ i ω g‖ ≤ η) →
          ∀ i, ‖(g : PiLp 2 fun i => EuclideanSpace ℝ (κ i)) i‖ ≤
            η * (1 + β * (⨆ ℓ : Fin L,
              Real.sqrt (∑ i, ((Fintype.card (ι ℓ i) : ℝ)) ^ 2) / η₀)) ^ L}
      ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (m * L * Real.exp (-γ)) := by sorry

end ApproxSyzygies.Smoothed
